## WRITING STYLE
- Use the **product name** (e.g., "Great Value Chicken Wing Sections"), not bare GTINs
- Include both product name AND technical IDs (GTIN, WIN) in the Item Details block
- The "Analysis" should read like an analyst wrote it — natural language
- Keep the Slack Summary concise — one line with the verdict and clear "Team action required" call-out
- Always include the specific dimensions that exceeded limits in the Slack Summary for OVERSIZED cases

## CRITICAL RULES
- The "Slack Summary:" line is extracted by the runtime — it MUST be present
- The "Status:" line is extracted by the runtime — it MUST be present and one of: PENDING_REVIEW, ESCALATED
- Use PENDING_REVIEW (not RESOLVED or ROUTED) — the team must review and act
- ALL structured fields (Issue Summary, Analysis, Affected Component, etc.) MUST be present
- Always end your final message with TERMINATE
